-- title:
--   Regularity descends along a finite étale local extension
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative ring which is local and Noetherian, and let $B'$ be a commutative local ring equipped with the structure of a $B$-algebra, subject to the following assumptions: $B'$ is finite as a $B$-module; the scalar action of $B$ on $B'$ is faithful, i.e. the structure map $B \to B'$ is injective; the algebra $B \to B'$ is étale; and $B'$ is a regular local ring. The conclusion is that $B$ is itself a regular local ring, that is, the maximal ideal of $B$ is generated by a number of elements equal to the Krull dimension of $B$. Note that no residue-field or separability condition beyond étaleness is imposed, and $B'$ is not assumed Noetherian separately, this being a consequence of module-finiteness over the Noetherian ring $B$.
--
--   This is the descent direction of the standard result that regularity is insensitive to finite étale local extensions (a special case of the transfer of regularity along flat local maps with regular closed fibre). It is used in the project to descend regularity from a Kummer-type étale cover, and is cited by [`IsRegularLocalRing.exists_isUnit_pow_eq_mul_of_baseChange`](thm.html#IsRegularLocalRing.exists_isUnit_pow_eq_mul_of_baseChange).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsRegularLocalRing_of_etale_of_moduleFinite.lean

